  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Hub, thesis, write path, read side",
      "items": [
        "Why LLM Wikis Beat RAG is the thesis: synthesis moves to ingest time, so knowledge compounds instead of being re-derived per query; the economics are maintenance, not retrieval.",
        "Three-Layer Architecture is the hub: immutable raw/, an agent-owned wiki/, and a schema that disciplines the agent.",
        "Ingest Workflow is the write path, one source per session with the user in the loop; Progressive Disclosure is the read side, where index.md routes but is not where the agent reasons."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "The comparators",
      "items": [
        "Skill Evolution (WikiSkill) swaps documents for traces and the schema for skills, and is the only controlled evidence for compounding: 63.7% vs 48.7%.",
        "Belief Ledger (gbrain) asks what markdown plus git fails to record; the page files it as a wiki-layer property, not a fourth layer.",
        "Provenance Tags sets obsidian-wiki's origin tags and OpenWiki's evidence ranges against claim callouts; Unattended Agent State is the discipline a timer-driven /scout would need.",
        "Every comparator so far changes the gate, not the layers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Where the tensions are",
      "items": [
        "Interactive gate vs mechanical maintenance: ingest stays interactive, but the maintenance claim rests on OpenWiki and WikiSkill, which run with no human at ingest. Filed speculative: a choice of gate, not of scale.",
        "Who reads the wiki: giving the executing agent wiki access lowered skill quality (63.7% to 60.9%), against the read-time-asset premise.",
        "Index vs embeddings: obsidian-wiki measured 44% vs 83% on graph questions; the index is a routing aid only.",
        "Inference lint cannot see prose: origin-mark lint only counts inference the agent admitted to."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Sourcing",
      "items": [
        "One paper carries the thesis: everything resting on WikiSkill is medium confidence from one paper, one model, three runs.",
        "obsidian-wiki's \"2000 pages, same cost\" is asserted, not shown. A second controlled study on a document corpus would move the compounding claim most.",
        "Fractal Federation and Subtractive Onboarding describe the template, not the sources: no sources, no callouts."
      ]
    }
  ]
}